# Ping thread

https://gitlab.com/scout-gg/croupier/-/work_items/1

Loading this rule is not a GitLab check. Do not check the thread on every user
turn and never poll in a loop.

Use `/ping-croupier` only when:

- Jakob explicitly asks whether Kevin replied or invokes `/ping-croupier`;
- a substantial Croupier stage is about to start and Kevin's answer can change
  its scope;
- a tested stage is ready for handoff or an integration decision, unless the
  thread was already checked during that checkpoint.

Perform at most one implicit check per checkpoint. After sending Kevin a note,
do not immediately poll for a reply; check at the next eligible checkpoint.
For an implicit check, stay silent when nothing changed. If a new note is
authored by `Kevinnegash1`, give one short, relevant summary. Never describe
another author's note as Kevin's reply.

Use GitLab `save_note` only when Jakob asks to send something
(`project_id: scout-gg/croupier`, `work_item_iid: 1`). Mention
`@Kevinnegash1` or `@Jakeminator123`, ask one short question, and do not start
a line with `/`.
